  <h1>Acme Engineering Monthly</h1>

  <h2>1. Password hygiene for teams</h2>
  <p>Never share your password or authenticator codes with anyone, including IT.
  Our security team will never ask for them by email.</p>

  <h2>2. Rotating API keys</h2>
  <p>Store API keys in a secrets manager, not in source code. Rotate them every 90 days
  and revoke keys you no longer use.</p>

  <h2>3. What is prompt injection?</h2>
  <p>Attackers hide phrases like "ignore previous instructions" inside web pages or
  emails to trick AI assistants. In this article we explain how our team detects
  these attacks and why you should treat retrieved content as data, not commands.</p>

  <h2>4. Release notes</h2>
  <p>Version 4.2 ships with a faster dashboard. You can ignore the old setup guide;
  the previous steps are no longer needed.</p>

  <p>Unsubscribe any time from your account settings.</p>
